{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"20d6db109c5245f0d03828e22afe11029eb0625ffca5e8d1681528c45c9cb4bf","occurred_at":"2026-11-21T17:23:27Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[222,223]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py","quoted_text":"        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=qcow2\" % (run / \"overlay.qcow2\"),\n        \"-drive\", \"file=%s,if=virtio,format=raw,readonly=on\" % (run / \"seed.iso\"),","reason":"QEMU's -drive option parser treats commas as option separators. Both drive arguments interpolate run/overlay.qcow2 and run/seed.iso directly without doubling embedded commas or rejecting comma-containing paths, so a state directory such as probe,local produces malformed -drive options and VM launch fails. This is an ordinary correctness bug in the existing qemu_command behavior, not a new hardening requirement.","target":"bc1f20eae782c27269f6d6cc4ad32db64889ea7f"},"finding_id":"9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568","previous_event_id":"f6ab2762cdcfe476a17249dfa7cbfb851f3e450be5f5bf5cb339c8086b281d4c","review_id":"f1b5131645f96822be0f07c1707f2cbcab3333693f6cab11de508eb6e932b92d"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:9b642ae652878daefd8f448658e4ed6ac5edf599d989d795ceb782a903115568:d7360649396bf1845f68c8d07739b2cb71d5c16aebb56e1afcb1b1baae1d25cd"}